WEBVTT

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:05.440
Perfect.

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:07.120
Way to go, Sango!

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:09.260
You're really good at sports!

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:11.480
I wonder how close I can get to 300.

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:18.320
Perfect.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.160
Aw, crap.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:24.160
Close one, Kujira.

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:31.170
Again?!

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:33.170
Can't get the spare, huh?

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:36.670
Want me to show you
how to bowl a strike?

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:41.650
You guys better not have
messed with these balls.

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:50.440
Hey, you sexy idiot.

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:51.940
Don't make me ban you!

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:52.690
Get out of here!

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:55.150
Why should I?

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:08.890
What's with that aim?

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:10.420
I'm sorry.

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:12.500
Watch your goddamn mouth.

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:13.670
Who the hell do you think you are?

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:18.490
I guess it <i>is true that guys who suck
blame their tools instead of themselves.</i>

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:22.260
Oh, aren't you so high and mighty.

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:23.800
You wanna fight, huh?

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:28.730
Aw, what happened?

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:31.600
Not much bite, pretty boy.

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:34.360
I'm going to kill you!

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.300
Would you shut up?

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:38.400
You're disturbing everyone around us.

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:48.420
Don't do anything stupid.

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:50.040
Yeah, yeah.

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:51.870
I'm just gonna have a little fun.

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:53.880
No... Y-You're kidding, right?

00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:56.380
...C-C'mon...

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:57.820
Don't do this!

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:13.020
I will carry my indomitable hope into the dark night

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:13.020
yami no naka no shinjitsu ga hikari kagayaku you ni

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:19.310
so that it may light a shining fire of truth there

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:19.310
kagi no nai kibou wo tokihanatou

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:34.760
I was born bleeding from my hands,

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:34.760
naze te no hira no kizu wo daite umareochita imi

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:38.750
and why was I born not a thousand years in the past or the future,

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:38.750
sennen kako demo mirai demo naku

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:40.060
but in the present?

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:40.060
erabareta ima

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:44.410
The scales of justice are fragile

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:44.410
zen'aku hakaru tenbin wa zeijaku

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:49.470
The waning, waxing moon calls to a flower on the earth

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:49.470
michikakeru tsuki ga izanau gisei no chi ni saita

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:51.370
the color of blood

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:51.370
chi no iro no hana

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:53.870
I will give all I have

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:53.870
tatta hitotsu kanau nara

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:56.570
if it means one of my wishes will come true

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:56.570
subete wo sasageyou

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:59.850
I have a "post nubila phoebus" kind of personality

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:59.850
post nubila phoebus kokoro

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:01.700
which I will show the world

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:01.700
kaze ni hanatte

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:04.700
I want to slash apart the curtain of raven black,

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:04.700
shikkoku no curtain hikichigiri

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:07.390
and look at a new world

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:07.390
chigau sora wo mitemitai

00:03:07.390 --> 00:03:10.060
My love stabs at the cracks

00:03:07.390 --> 00:03:10.060
sabita unmei no hibiware

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:12.530
of a stagnant fate

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:12.530
omoi wa nejikonde

00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:15.390
No matter how long the storm lasts,

00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:15.390
donnani arasoi tsuzuketemo

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:18.000
time itself will not stop breathing

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:18.000
toki wa kokyuu wo yamenai

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:20.760
What remains after destruction, rebirth,

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:20.760
kowashite tsunde kowashite

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:23.230
and further destruction?

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:23.230
nani ga nokoru darou

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:25.960
I'm sure I can put an end to a thousand nights of doubt

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:25.960
sou nanajuuokuban no mayoi mo

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:29.100
and to the system of the world

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:29.100
sono haichizu wa kakikaerareru

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:31.770
I'm sure that one day I will find a place where I can shine

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:31.770
moetsukitemo kagayakeru basho e

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:36.010
even if only ashes will remain

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:36.010
itsuka tadoritsukeru

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:39.990
Butterfly Law Offices

00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:39.990
Your lunch looks pretty good today.

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:44.070
I told Nana Genie that if he made another
one of those sexual harassment lunches,

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:48.000
Six Nine

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:48.000
Case 5

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:45.810
I'd smack him in the head six times.

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:48.000
Those were pretty funny, though.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.610
How do you stay so thin?

00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:54.670
I have no idea.

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:56.990
Come on, Kiri.

00:03:56.990 --> 00:03:59.180
Can you do your job?

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:04.530
You haven't finished any of the
documents I asked you to do.

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:08.410
I need to take those to the
Court for Magic tomorrow.

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:10.370
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:13.970
You forget things very easily
when you're older.

00:04:13.970 --> 00:04:16.350
Fine. I'll just do them myself.

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:18.190
Don't worry about it.

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:21.200
You never see Tsunomin
getting that mad.

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:26.490
Just remember that when Tsunomin's
really mad, she's the scariest person here.

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:27.700
I see.

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:30.210
...And yet...

00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:34.270
Kiri is in his own little world.

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:35.710
Cecil!

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:37.210
Come here.

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:43.220
I've already discussed
the matter with Seseri,

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:46.350
but I actually have
...a request for you, Cecil—

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:48.130
I can't!

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:50.230
I already told you the last time we met.

00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:54.910
I'd be too nervous to work at
Shark Knight because you're all male.

00:04:54.910 --> 00:04:57.290
And I'm happy working here, anyway.

00:04:57.290 --> 00:04:58.990
...I have no intentions of qui—

00:04:58.990 --> 00:05:00.740
I have a job for you.

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:05.340
Last night, my associate, Kujira Shibuki,

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:07.290
was arrested for murder.

00:05:07.290 --> 00:05:07.990
Huh?

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:11.130
Naturally, he denies this charge.

00:05:11.130 --> 00:05:14.130
I want you to defend him.

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:20.380
Oh, man. Shark Knight's
gonna owe us big time for this.

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:23.640
Why would they come and
ask the competition for help?

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:27.870
He said something about
acknowledging Cecil's abilities.

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:29.960
Th-That can't be it!

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:30.840
No way!

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:35.650
What a perfect opportunity to
go on a mixer with the Prince.

00:05:35.650 --> 00:05:38.380
Get your mind out
of the gutter, Sasorin.

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:40.650
This is work.

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:41.990
Exactly.

00:05:41.990 --> 00:05:46.350
You should be sent to space so you can
come to terms with your dirty thoughts!

00:05:46.350 --> 00:05:48.330
Keep talking like that,
and I'll fondle your boobs.

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:49.790
Not again! Don't you dare!

00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:52.910
So, who'll be Cecilcchi's partner?

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:56.420
Kiri, if you would.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:57.920
Huh?

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:02.680
I'd like you to work with Cecil
to defend Kujira of Shark Knight.

00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:03.920
Huh?

00:06:08.350 --> 00:06:11.510
You're <i>how old, and still
a working wizard barrister?</i>

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:13.480
Cecil would have been
more than enough.

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:15.670
...N-No...

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:20.850
We can't have you
seducing Cecil, you see.

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:24.740
There's no way I can
seduce her from jail, old man.

00:06:24.740 --> 00:06:27.240
So what exactly happened?

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:30.700
I was just pissed off.

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:35.570
So I went to the bowling alley and
used my powerspeak to control him.

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:38.730
I felt way better!

00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:41.810
Isn't that against the
magic-prohibition law?

00:06:43.180 --> 00:06:46.790
I'd say it was more
of a fight between kids.

00:06:46.790 --> 00:06:49.600
Is there really any reason
to involve the law?

00:06:50.170 --> 00:06:52.100
...Says a wizard barrister...

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:56.270
By the time I got back to
...the restaurant, the cops came...

00:06:56.270 --> 00:06:57.880
and, here I am.

00:06:58.630 --> 00:07:02.430
Right after I left the bowling alley,
the manager was killed.

00:07:03.160 --> 00:07:06.120
And you're denying
those charges, right?

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:07.620
Of course I am!

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:09.220
I didn't kill him!

00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:11.120
Is there anyone who can prove that?

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:12.410
No.

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:13.620
I'd like you to find someone.

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:14.950
All right.

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:17.670
So we have no alibi.

00:07:18.220 --> 00:07:20.750
The weapon used was some sort of knife.

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:23.530
But they weren't able to
find one at the scene.

00:07:23.530 --> 00:07:26.800
If I <i>wanted to kill someone,</i>

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:29.230
I wouldn't use something
as troublesome as a weapon.

00:07:29.230 --> 00:07:32.140
I'd use my powerspeak to
make it look like a suicide.

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:36.140
I did something stupid, and I regret it.

00:07:36.140 --> 00:07:39.650
But the police seem convinced
that I actually <i>killed the guy.</i>

00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:45.930
Before they indict me, please find some
evidence to help prove my innocence.

00:07:49.560 --> 00:07:51.390
...So they couldn't find the weapon...

00:07:51.390 --> 00:07:54.590
And the crime happened
...in a bowling alley bathroom...

00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:57.960
Circumstantially,
Kujira is at a disadvantage,

00:07:57.960 --> 00:08:00.310
but there isn't any physical evidence.

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:03.810
Huh?

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:08.220
Loveladol

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:08.220
Hand-Shaking Event!!

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:08.950
Good grief, what are you doing?!

00:08:08.950 --> 00:08:11.090
I'm a fan.

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:13.220
We've got work to do!

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:18.170
Well, he came into the bowling alley
and went right up to the manager.

00:08:18.170 --> 00:08:20.170
He yelled at him with
this angry look on his face.

00:08:20.170 --> 00:08:23.690
For some reason,
the manager started stripping.

00:08:23.690 --> 00:08:26.230
He burst out laughing
when he saw that, didn't he?

00:08:26.660 --> 00:08:30.990
That's when the manager regained
his senses and chased the suspect.

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:34.310
Who would've guessed
he'd be killed, though?

00:08:34.310 --> 00:08:36.740
Huh? The manager's acquaintances?

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:40.770
I'm not so sure.
We never really talked all that much.

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:48.010
The more people we interview, the more
Kujira seems to be at a disadvantage.

00:08:48.010 --> 00:08:51.290
Well, there's no point in hurrying.

00:08:51.290 --> 00:08:55.030
Yeah, but there isn't much time
before the indictment!

00:08:56.420 --> 00:08:58.290
Aren't you an eager one.

00:08:58.290 --> 00:09:01.020
Slow down, or I won't
be able to keep up with you.

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:04.770
I'm sixty-nine years older
than you, you know.

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:10.670
When you've been in the business as long as I have,
you know when to give it your all, and when to relax.

00:09:11.460 --> 00:09:16.280
You're way too tense, Cecil.

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:14.280
The new album from the girls you
love is here! With 8 new songs and
some anime tie-ins!

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:14.280
Long-Awaited New Album

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:19.330
...And you're not tense enough, Kiri...

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:24.490
Glory to Macal.

00:09:24.490 --> 00:09:26.850
Punish Labone.

00:09:26.850 --> 00:09:28.540
Prosperity to Macal.

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:31.830
May the humans suffer many years of pain.

00:09:31.830 --> 00:09:35.050
We cannot forget our
persecution at human hands,

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:39.560
nor the betrayal of the Labone.

00:09:40.020 --> 00:09:43.490
We shall show no mercy to those who
hinder our plan and to those who oppose us.

00:09:43.490 --> 00:09:46.090
Let us rid them of existence

00:09:46.090 --> 00:09:48.060
and fulfill the prophecy.

00:09:49.960 --> 00:09:53.750
Lord Makusu, what about the
wizard that Grimoire 365 mentions?

00:09:53.750 --> 00:09:57.770
The one that's said to only appear
once every few hundred years?

00:09:59.020 --> 00:10:00.830
Just as we planned,

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:05.330
Sudou Cecil is gradually
awakening to her dormant powers.

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:08.230
The fated time draws near.

00:10:28.340 --> 00:10:30.980
I guess there really <i>is</i>
no evidence to be found.

00:10:34.490 --> 00:10:36.820
Kiri, please get back to work!

00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:38.070
Huh?

00:10:38.520 --> 00:10:39.820
Please get back to work!

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:41.080
You know, work?

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:21.210
Sheesh.

00:11:21.210 --> 00:11:22.570
What on Earth are you doing?

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:24.490
The indictment is coming up!

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:28.090
Why did we even hire you people?!

00:11:28.090 --> 00:11:30.230
Just give us a few more days.

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:34.500
You young folk are always
in such a hurry to get results.

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:37.250
With the rest of your lives ahead of you,
there's no reason to be in such a hurry.

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:39.760
You're just too slow, you old fart!

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:43.260
A-Anyway, we'll get it together.

00:11:46.410 --> 00:11:47.520
...Kiri...

00:11:52.220 --> 00:11:55.770
Um, shouldn't we speed
things up just a little bit?

00:11:57.040 --> 00:12:01.780
I'm sorry for having
you work at my speed.

00:12:01.780 --> 00:12:05.450
We won't make it in time
for the indictment at this rate.

00:12:05.450 --> 00:12:06.790
So you <i>are having issues.</i>

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:10.790
The indictment will probably
be tomorrow or the day after.

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:13.040
Huh? Why so soon?

00:12:13.890 --> 00:12:15.890
Without any physical evidence,

00:12:15.890 --> 00:12:18.920
they'll go through with the indictment
based on the customer testimonies.

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:21.300
You know what that means,
don't you, Cecil?

00:12:23.380 --> 00:12:27.160
So if the testimonies lose credibility,

00:12:27.160 --> 00:12:30.290
they'll let the indictment go?

00:12:31.200 --> 00:12:36.660
Well, it's the prosecution's call
which testimony is used as evidence.

00:12:36.660 --> 00:12:39.100
Um, why are you telling us this?

00:12:39.100 --> 00:12:41.320
I like to fight fair.

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:42.320
Bye.

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:46.330
...Jeez, I'm beat...

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:51.010
Working at Kiri's speed
threw me off completely.

00:12:51.010 --> 00:12:53.550
Sounds like you had a rough time.

00:12:53.550 --> 00:12:55.730
I can see you're doing your best, Cecil.

00:12:55.730 --> 00:12:58.070
Huh? You're being pretty nice today.

00:12:58.070 --> 00:13:00.730
Finally understand how hard I work?

00:13:00.730 --> 00:13:02.350
Of course!

00:13:02.350 --> 00:13:05.050
You're amazing!

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:06.050
Gross.

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:06.810
...Something's off...

00:13:06.810 --> 00:13:08.790
Wh-What are you saying?

00:13:08.790 --> 00:13:10.600
I'm just doing this because
I recognize your efforts!

00:13:13.440 --> 00:13:14.440
It's gone!

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:17.940
The apple pie I was saving is gone!

00:13:18.820 --> 00:13:19.930
So mean!

00:13:19.930 --> 00:13:20.950
Stupid!

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:24.530
...I'm so hurt...

00:13:40.550 --> 00:13:43.050
Butterfly Law Offices

00:13:40.550 --> 00:13:43.050
No Parking of Cars or Bicycles

00:13:40.550 --> 00:13:43.050
Entrance and Exit for Business Vehicles Only

00:13:44.180 --> 00:13:47.110
Kujira's indictment has been decided.

00:13:48.300 --> 00:13:51.230
What have you been doing all this time?

00:13:52.830 --> 00:13:54.310
I'm sorry.

00:13:55.720 --> 00:13:57.630
...So they indicted him...

00:13:57.630 --> 00:14:01.970
If I have to deal with Kiri, I won't even be
able to obtain the documents I otherwise can.

00:14:01.970 --> 00:14:03.750
We won't make it in time for the trial!

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:06.820
So you want Kiri off the case?

00:14:09.460 --> 00:14:12.090
This case is too much
for just one person to take.

00:14:12.090 --> 00:14:13.830
Kiri has experience.

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:16.410
And that's what you lack the most.

00:14:17.200 --> 00:14:21.090
I don't think experience is the
only important factor, though.

00:14:21.740 --> 00:14:23.790
Learn on the job.

00:14:23.790 --> 00:14:25.470
I can't change your partner.

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:34.870
Who do you think you are?

00:14:37.600 --> 00:14:38.780
...Natcchi...

00:14:38.780 --> 00:14:42.110
You're in no position to say
you want Kamakiri off the case.

00:14:42.920 --> 00:14:47.610
This is my case,
and I want to do the best I can.

00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:48.750
Excuse me?

00:14:48.750 --> 00:14:50.620
Get off your high horse.

00:14:51.020 --> 00:14:53.110
Sure, you may have become
a wizard barrister at seventeen,

00:14:53.110 --> 00:14:55.370
and yes, everyone recognizes
how talented you are,

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:58.250
but you <i>do realize that you didn't
achieve all of this alone, right?</i>

00:14:58.250 --> 00:15:00.630
That's not what I'm saying!

00:15:00.630 --> 00:15:05.250
Why can't you see that Kamakiri
is <i>helping you on this case?</i>

00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:11.510
How is he helping me
when all he does is slack off?

00:15:11.510 --> 00:15:13.330
He may be slow,

00:15:13.330 --> 00:15:15.390
but he does great work.

00:15:15.390 --> 00:15:17.390
Not to mention, he understands people.

00:15:17.390 --> 00:15:20.650
I bet he's long since realized that
you hold some animosity toward him.

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:26.790
You have a big mouth for someone
who can only see the obvious.

00:15:28.640 --> 00:15:32.670
Still, it doesn't feel like
Kiri's being serious at all.

00:15:32.670 --> 00:15:34.410
I can't stand it anymore.

00:15:34.750 --> 00:15:37.660
You don't understand
how I feel, Natcchi!

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:40.170
Why don't you try partnering
with Kiri sometime?

00:15:41.560 --> 00:15:43.380
We're all on the same team.

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:45.850
You should know better
than to get into serious fights.

00:15:45.850 --> 00:15:48.920
I've never seen Sudou take
that much offense to something.

00:15:49.980 --> 00:15:52.930
Oh, good morning, Cecil.

00:15:52.930 --> 00:15:54.390
Good morning?

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:55.930
...It's already noon...

00:15:56.860 --> 00:16:00.940
I stayed up to watch
a late-night idol show.

00:16:00.940 --> 00:16:02.330
...Again with the idols...

00:16:02.330 --> 00:16:03.410
Oh, right.

00:16:03.410 --> 00:16:06.670
There's something
I want to show you.

00:16:06.670 --> 00:16:09.170
I don't want to see any
idol photo collections!

00:16:09.950 --> 00:16:12.700
...It's this month's shift schedule...

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:17.690
While I was up, I got it from
the bowling alley's garbage can.

00:16:17.690 --> 00:16:18.820
...This is...

00:16:18.820 --> 00:16:20.710
Take a look at this here.

00:16:20.710 --> 00:16:25.710
These two have the same shifts,
and the exact same days off.

00:16:26.560 --> 00:16:32.970
I was a bit curious, so I asked one of the
employees to show me an older schedule,

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:35.750
and it was exactly the same.

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:35.970
Suzui Hiroyuki

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:35.970
Kiritani Takuma

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:35.970
March Schedule

00:16:36.500 --> 00:16:37.970
What does that mean, though?

00:16:38.340 --> 00:16:42.470
Remember what this employee told us?

00:16:43.620 --> 00:16:45.950
Huh? The manager's acquaintances?

00:16:46.520 --> 00:16:50.610
I'm not so sure.
We never really talked all that much.

00:16:50.690 --> 00:16:54.700
A manager and employee
that didn't talk much,

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:57.150
but work the same shifts every day?

00:16:57.150 --> 00:17:02.570
Surely this can't be just a coincidence.

00:17:02.570 --> 00:17:03.710
...Also...

00:17:03.710 --> 00:17:07.290
They used to work overtime a lot.

00:17:07.290 --> 00:17:11.720
I remember seeing them
whisper to each other.

00:17:11.720 --> 00:17:14.220
Contradicts the testimony, doesn't it?

00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:17.820
But why that employee?

00:17:17.820 --> 00:17:20.720
I don't remember anything
suspicious about him.

00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:25.550
It's just a hunch from
doing this for oh so many years.

00:17:27.610 --> 00:17:32.090
Oh, Suzui has been
taking some time off lately.

00:17:32.090 --> 00:17:35.610
I also heard he was going to quit.

00:17:38.960 --> 00:17:40.620
What do you want?

00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:45.130
The fact that the manager and I had
the same shifts is just a coincidence.

00:17:45.130 --> 00:17:50.630
So you two weren't doing anything
together on your days off, then?

00:17:56.640 --> 00:17:58.130
...O-Of course not...

00:17:58.130 --> 00:18:00.760
Quit with the baseless accusations!

00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:11.250
Will the schedule alone
be enough evidence?

00:18:11.250 --> 00:18:13.390
Most likely not.

00:18:14.300 --> 00:18:15.270
Kiri!

00:18:15.270 --> 00:18:19.610
All that means is we need to
create some evidence ourselves.

00:18:32.900 --> 00:18:34.050
Wh-What?

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:45.930
...M-Manager...

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:47.790
You're supposed to be dead!

00:18:47.790 --> 00:18:49.440
St-Stay back!

00:18:50.180 --> 00:18:51.940
I-It wasn't my fault!

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:55.510
This is all because you were
trying to take everything for yourself!

00:19:01.220 --> 00:19:02.170
St-Stay back!

00:19:02.170 --> 00:19:03.570
...If you come any closer...

00:19:03.570 --> 00:19:05.770
So that must be the weapon.

00:19:09.300 --> 00:19:10.460
Y-You!

00:19:10.940 --> 00:19:13.460
Cecil, did you record that?

00:19:14.200 --> 00:19:15.220
Got it!

00:19:19.160 --> 00:19:21.800
This knife is the murder weapon.

00:19:22.260 --> 00:19:29.340
And you just heard Suzui's motive and plan
for the murder straight from his own mouth.

00:19:29.670 --> 00:19:33.450
It has also been proven that the victim,
Kiritani, and Suzui were thieves,

00:19:34.070 --> 00:19:38.570
and that they had a falling out
which lead to the victim's murder.

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:47.330
What were the DNA test results from
the blood sample taken from the knife?

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:51.170
They matched that
of the victim, Kiritani.

00:19:51.170 --> 00:19:55.340
Therefore, the defendant,
Kujira Shibuki, is innocent!

00:19:55.780 --> 00:19:57.840
What will the prosecution do?

00:19:58.500 --> 00:20:00.220
We withdraw our indictment.

00:20:00.600 --> 00:20:01.720
All right!

00:20:02.840 --> 00:20:04.220
...However...

00:20:04.220 --> 00:20:06.770
There's one thing that's
off about this evidence.

00:20:07.540 --> 00:20:12.970
It seems likely that the barrister
used magic to get the suspect to confess.

00:20:13.880 --> 00:20:17.170
Did the defense use magic?

00:20:19.920 --> 00:20:21.690
Respond quickly!

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:32.790
Kiri!

00:20:33.440 --> 00:20:36.040
Wake up, Kiri!

00:20:38.140 --> 00:20:40.050
How is Kamakiri doing?

00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:42.170
They're examining him now.

00:20:42.170 --> 00:20:44.150
...That old man does good work...

00:20:44.150 --> 00:20:45.470
I'm impressed.

00:20:47.300 --> 00:20:49.710
Thank you very much.

00:20:49.710 --> 00:20:51.310
Please allow me to
also thank you personally.

00:20:52.120 --> 00:20:56.190
I really <i>would love to work
with someone as talented as you.</i>

00:20:56.190 --> 00:20:58.190
You can come by our office at any time.

00:20:58.970 --> 00:21:01.070
...I'm still inexperienced...

00:21:01.070 --> 00:21:04.070
I think you know that now, Sameoka.

00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:08.330
So why is it that you'd want me?

00:21:14.140 --> 00:21:14.910
Hello?

00:21:14.910 --> 00:21:16.290
Cecil!

00:21:16.290 --> 00:21:19.410
Just leave Kiri there
and head back to the office.

00:21:19.410 --> 00:21:20.590
...Huh? But...

00:21:20.590 --> 00:21:22.110
Right now!

00:21:25.140 --> 00:21:27.220
Oh, Cecilun, welcome back!

00:21:27.900 --> 00:21:29.720
Good work at the trial.

00:21:30.100 --> 00:21:34.570
As a reward, I'll take you to the
Ueno hot stone bath, Cecilcchi.

00:21:34.570 --> 00:21:35.870
Let me come too!

00:21:35.870 --> 00:21:37.230
Me too!

00:21:38.380 --> 00:21:41.990
Aren't you guys worried about Kiri?

00:21:41.990 --> 00:21:44.370
He's all alone at the hospital.

00:21:44.370 --> 00:21:47.550
How come none of you visited?

00:21:47.550 --> 00:21:49.490
That's terrible! He's one of us!

00:21:49.490 --> 00:21:51.570
You don't know?

00:21:51.570 --> 00:21:52.970
He's faking it.

00:21:53.750 --> 00:21:56.000
When things get bad during the trial,

00:21:56.000 --> 00:21:58.500
he passes out so they'll close the case.

00:21:59.120 --> 00:22:00.250
...No way...

00:22:06.800 --> 00:22:09.550
...Dancing, dancing...

00:22:25.970 --> 00:22:32.910
My heart may cry silently,

00:22:25.970 --> 00:22:32.910
kokoro ga donna ni namida afuretemo

00:22:33.310 --> 00:22:40.470
but I still want to behold the blue sky

00:22:33.310 --> 00:22:40.470
hitomi ni aozora utsushiteitai

00:22:40.710 --> 00:22:48.040
I want to have something like the strength of flowers

00:22:40.710 --> 00:22:48.040
concrete-iro no machi no katasumi ni

00:22:48.040 --> 00:22:55.440
which bloom in the nooks of the endless concrete of the city

00:22:48.040 --> 00:22:55.440
sotto saku hana no tsuyosa wo manetai

00:22:55.440 --> 00:23:02.870
Starting today, I won't try to wriggle out by saying

00:22:55.440 --> 00:23:02.870
maegami ga jama de mienai nante iiwake

00:23:02.870 --> 00:23:06.710
that I saw nothing because my hair was in the way

00:23:02.870 --> 00:23:06.710
kyou kara shinai

00:23:07.660 --> 00:23:15.150
Beyond the horizon, my future awaits me,

00:23:07.660 --> 00:23:15.150
chiheisen no mukou ni ashita ga matteru kara

00:23:15.150 --> 00:23:20.370
so I will let the sun in my heart

00:23:15.150 --> 00:23:20.370
kono mune no hitotsu no taiyou

00:23:20.370 --> 00:23:22.420
shine out far and wide

00:23:20.370 --> 00:23:22.420
tooku hanatte

00:23:22.420 --> 00:23:29.790
I will overtake the earth's rotation on the path I walk,

00:23:22.420 --> 00:23:29.790
chikyuu no jiten wo oikosu kurai hitamuki ni arukou

00:23:29.790 --> 00:23:37.880
with trusting love inside my heart

00:23:29.790 --> 00:23:37.880
shinjiru omoi dakishimete doko made mo
